# Lesson3 — HOST-LOCAL development template (`npx next dev` on your own machine).
#
# Copy to `app/.env` (gitignored) and fill in. This file is deliberately SMALL: it carries only what
# a host-local run must set differently from a container. For the complete documented reference —
# every rate-limit, email, jobs, cache and ops variable with its default — see the canonical
# **`../.env.example`** at the repo root.
#
# What is DECLARED here is everything required to boot. What is omitted still has a default — but not
# always one that suits a host-local run: `GOTENBERG_URL` defaults to `http://gotenberg:3000`, a Compose
# service name that does not resolve from the host, so PDF conversion fails until you set it (see the
# optional section below).
#
# ⚑ This is NOT the Compose template and must not become a copy of one. It was: until 2026-08-05 it
# pointed DATABASE_URI at `postgres:5432` (the Compose service host, unreachable from the host) and
# declared Compose-only POSTGRES_PASSWORD, which means nothing to a host-local run.
# `tests/unit/envTemplateParity.spec.ts` now enforces both halves — nothing here the app doesn't
# read, and a localhost DB host.
#
# Full local-stack procedure (start Postgres, seed roles + one browsable lesson plan):
# AGENTS.md → Local stack.

# The local stack publishes Postgres on 127.0.0.1:55432 — `docker-compose.local.yml`, opt-in via
# `-f`, deliberately NOT named docker-compose.override.yml (Compose auto-loads that on EVERY
# invocation including scripts/deploy.sh, which would silently publish the database on a deployed
# box). Containers are unaffected: they read the root `.env` and reach `postgres:5432` internally.
DATABASE_URI=postgres://lesson3:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:55432/lesson3

# Long random string — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Base URL for links in outbound email. `next dev` serves on 3000 (the Compose app is on 3001).
ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Leave EMPTY for local development. Setting it enables strict CSRF + Secure cookies, neither of
# which suits plain-HTTP localhost. Full explanation of the switch: ../.env.example.
SERVER_URL=

# ───────────────── Optional locally — defaults are correct for dev ─────────────────

# Only needed to exercise PDF export locally with a Gotenberg sidecar of your own. Unset, PDF
# conversion fails fast and DOCX export is unaffected.
# GOTENBERG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3002

# Only needed to work on the PUBLIC lesson library locally. Unset (the default), /explore 404s and
# /login shows no Explore action — which is also what an offline school deployment runs.
#
# ⚑ Enabling it REQUIRES SERVER_URL above, or the app refuses to boot. For local work that means
# setting both, e.g. SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000 — but note SERVER_URL also turns on strict
# CSRF and Secure cookies, which do not suit plain-HTTP localhost, so expect to sign in over
# https or to work on the public pages while signed out. Rationale: ../.env.example.
# PUBLIC_LIBRARY_ENABLED=1

# Unset outside Docker the artifact cache falls back to a local ./.artifact-cache, which is the
# right dev behaviour. Set it only to relocate that cache.
# ARTIFACT_CACHE_DIR=

# Proof-of-concept PDF link library for host-local development. The production Compose stack uses
# /var/lib/lesson3-resources, mounted read-only from ../out/resource-library.
PDF_LIBRARY_DIR=../out/resource-library

# LOG_LEVEL=debug for verbose Payload logging; RENDER_TIMINGS=1 for one-off render timings.
# LOG_LEVEL=info
